      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A novel copper-catalyzed N-oxide oxidation of N-sulfonyl ynamides is disclosed. This non-noble metal-catalyzed protocol enables facile and efficient access to valuable α-keto imides in generally good to excellent yields. Other notable features of this method include widespread availability of the substrates, compatibility with broad functional groups, a simple procedure, mild conditions, and in particular, no need to exclude moisture or air (\"open flask\")."},
